--- stdout
Compile a Spago workspace from an entry point to a single Go program.

Usage: iris go [FLAGS] [DIR]

Arguments:
  [DIR]  Directory to write main.go to. Without one, builds the executable that `iris run --go` runs and prints its
         path.

Flags:
  -p, --package <NAME>       Workspace package to compile.
      --entry <MODULE.NAME>  Qualified entry point. Defaults to Main.main, or without DIR to the one `iris run --go`
                             uses.
      --no-line-directives   Leaves out of the Go written to DIR the //line comments that make stack traces, debuggers
                             and profiles point at your .purs files.
  -h, --help                 Print help
--- stderr
